Z||000000||Dale||08-19-99||12:49 PM||||Minor overheating problem (not).  I have an 84 se 4 cyl.  The cooling fan is not coming on.  Can anyone tell me where the relay switch, fuse, fusable link, sensor is on this thing.  I know where the temp gauge and computer temp sensors are but thanks to HAYNES they give no clue where the other stuff is.  If I wouldnt have to stop for traffic I would be fine.<p>Mahalo
Z||000001||DJRice||08-19-99||12:55 PM||||The fan relay is under the drivers side headlight area.  It should only cost you about $10. 
Z||000002||Dale||08-19-99||01:11 PM||||Thanks DJ I will check it out.  I forgot to mention the fan wont come on when you turn the AC on either.  I believe it is supposed to automaticaly
Z||000003||DJRice||08-19-99||01:55 PM||||Your right, it should come on when the AC is on.  Try the relay first, but if that does not fix it, the fan motor itself could be bad, that happens from time to time.
Z||000004||TOM||08-19-99||04:08 PM||||My fan also had a problem of not coming on with the a/c. I found it was a burnt cuircut in the a/c control head. I replaced it for $10 and now all is fine.
